2026-09-27T10:00:41.3515945Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3516280Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3516561Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3517165Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3518046Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3518150Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3518376Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3518683Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3518973Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3519104Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3519331Z ================
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3519434Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3519692Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3520064Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3520290Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3520445Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3520777Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3520983Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3521155Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3521557Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3521999Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3522729Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3523224Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3523381Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3523845Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3524433Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3524770Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3525072Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3525523Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3525616Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3525910Z ========
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3526033Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3527756Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3528939Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3529207Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3529741Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3530620Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3531835Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3532438Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3532926Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3533422Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3533547Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3533861Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3534053Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3535007Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3536046Z 
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3536637Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3537269Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:00:41.3537461Z 
